            <ArticleTitle>Analgesic drug therapy in cancer pain: principles and practice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>207-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Drug therapy represents the mainstay of treatment for patients with cancer pain. Non-narcotic, narcotic, and adjuvant analgesics are the commonly used agents. The choice of a specific analgesic drug regimen is dependent on the type of pain and its severity, and the drug must be titrated to the individual needs of the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
